# The build context of docs.Dockerfile (BuildKit reads this file for it, in place of .dockerignore, which is the API's
# image's and leaves docs/ out). Only what the Hugo site is built from comes in: the site (docs/), the two files it
# renders at the repository's root (CHANGELOG.md and CONTRIBUTING.md, mounted by docs/hugo.toml), and the history
# enableGitInfo reads (.git). The coverage report is part of docs/: the deploy copies it in before the build.
*
!docs
!CHANGELOG.md
!CONTRIBUTING.md
!.git

# Not part of the site, or rebuilt by the image.
docs/node_modules
docs/public
docs/resources
docs/.hugo_build.lock
docs/themes
